so I'm sure you've been razzle dazzled  by the hunter and its golden gun for the  warlock with its nova bombs I'm here to  tell you that the Titan is the Hulk of  the Guardians remember what the hole did  to Loki yeah that's what the Titan will  give you if that doesn't pique your  interest then the Titans second subclass  the defender makes you the ultimate tank  for you and your teammate if you want to  become a Titan here's more about both of  its subclasses starting subclass where  the Titan is a striker the striker is  the more offensive of the two subclasses  and gives you the ability to clear out  enemies with ease the striker special  move is the fist of havoc which is a  leaping ground slam that kills foes  within the blast radius this of havoc is  especially good for clearing out waves  of minions during an objective hold or  during a boss battle in addition this  skill is greatly useful in the crucible  as it allows you to take out multiple  Guardians that are clustered together  especially in the control zone game type  with our big areas of contention be  careful when using this ability at low  health though because there will be  times when you'll die during the casting  animation and then you'll lose your  overcharge another aspect that  differentiates the subclasses organ AIDS  the Titans primary grenade is a  flashbang that disorients your enemies  you'll know that that are flash because  they'll have a red cloud over their head  that make them easy targets to close in  on with a shotgun or a melee strike the  secondary grenade is a pulse grenade  which periodically damages enemies  inside its explosion radius this grenade  doesn't seem a strong though because  it's easily avoidable finish off any  stragglers with your strong melee  ability of the storm fist which seals  bonus melee damage watch the cooldown on  storm fist though or you won't pack that  extra wallop you normally do you can  even turn yourself into a juggernaut so  to speak as you run you'll pick up  momentum and once you've acquired a  target let your melee trigger rip and  send your opponent's flying with a  running shoulder tackle the shoulder  tackle is an upgrade further along in  the Stryker skill tree if this style  doesn't suit you choose a more defensive  support subclass of the Titan the  defender the defender special is the  ward of dawn which creates a large  bubble that is impenetrable to bullets  rockets lasers and more use this to  revive your fallen teammates for in a  pinch when you're surrounded and running  low on health the ward of dawn can be  upgraded to last longer and later down  the road it can buff your teammates as  well  the only drawback to the ward of dawn is  you can't shoot from within the bubble  however if the enemies walk into the  bubble  you can melee them with no fear as  you'll stay relatively invulnerable this  is a good tactic when being surrounded  by lesser mobs let them walk in and play  Rock'em Sock'em robots even more reason  to kill your opponents with your melee  ability is the fact that the defenders  melee skill disintegrates gives you a  force barrier that absorbs incoming  damage you'll know you have this active  by your glowing purple hand this skill  can also be used in a pinch as well to  help you stay alive if you're low on  health as the shield effect will mask  your low life the interesting thing  about the defender is the grenade  ability it gets the magnetic grenade  sticks to either the enemy or the  surface that you threw it at and  explodes twice the grenade can then be  upgraded to shoot out a void of light or  charges of energy you can stick these  grenades in any direction horizontal  vertical or diagonal depending on how  you throw it this can then be used to  zone out mobs or players in PvP the  tanks double jump is the same for both  subclasses and on first upgrade allows  you to ascend higher into the air this  skill is subpar because you end up  floating in the air making you an easy  target to pick off the upgraded  controlled double jump is much better  however as it allows you to control  which direction you want to boost you in  the air this is especially good if you  know a rocket or big damage is coming to  your side as you can boost your way into  the other direction the time class gives  you the flexibility to play two very  distinct styles they'll cater to your  needs or to the needs at hand  just make sure whichever one you're more  interested in is the one you level first  as you have to level these separately in  addition when you first pick up the  defender subclass you'll have to start  leveling from scratch that's right no  double jump or grenades right off the  bat to help level the freshly unlocked  defender subclass complete bounties as a  striker but then switch to the defender  before cashing them in whatever class  weapons and gear you have equipped when  you're actually turning your bounties  will receive the XP boost as well it'll  be interesting to see if the defender  becomes more useful when raids come out  as a difficulty will likely increase  with more players and enemies in the mix  as currently I personally still prefer  the striker subclass because who doesn't  want to channel their inner Hulk this is  the fight it's a mess  you
 

